{:edb/db-before-t 1600 :edb/db-after-t 1601 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534913 50 #inst "2026-10-08T10:50:07.329Z" 13194139534913 true] [17592186078233 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\dfrac {\\textrm d} {\\textrm dx} \\int_2^x \\dfrac {t^3} {t-1}\\,\\textrm d t$ for $x>2$." 13194139534913 false] [17592186078233 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\dfrac {\\textrm d} {\\textrm dx} \\int_2^x \\dfrac {t^3} {t-1}\\,\\textrm d t$ for $x>2.$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186078233 1145 "The function\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {t^3} {t-1}\n$$\n\nis continuous on $[2,x]$, where $x>2$. So FTC II applies, and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{d}{dx}∫_{2}^{x}\\frac{t^{3}}{t - 1}dt = \\frac{x^{3}}{x - 1}\n$$" 13194139534913 false] [17592186078233 1145 "The function $\\dfrac {t^3} {t-1}$ is continuous on $[2,x],$ where $x>2.$ So FTC II applies, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{{t}^{3}}{t-1}\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186078234 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\dfrac {\\textrm d} {\\textrm dx} \\int_x^0  \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1}\\,\\textrm d t.$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186078234 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\dfrac {\\textrm d} {\\textrm dx} \\int_x^0 \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1}\\,\\textrm d t$." 13194139534913 false] [17592186078234 1145 "In this example, the variable limit $x$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int_x^0 \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1} \\,\\textrm d t  = -  \\int_0^x \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1}\\,\\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n \\displaystyle\\dfrac {\\textrm d} {\\textrm dx} \\int_x^0  \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1} \\,\\textrm d t \n\t& \\, \\, = \\, \\, \\dfrac {\\textrm d} {\\textrm dx} \\left(-\\int_0^x \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1} \\,\\textrm d t \\right)\\\n\t& \\, \\, = \\, \\, -\\dfrac {\\textrm d} {\\textrm dx} \\left(\\int_0^x \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1} \\,\\textrm d t \\right)\\\n\t&= \\, \\, -\\dfrac{x^3}{x^2 +1}.}\n$$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186078234 1145 "In this example, the variable limit $x$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int_x^0 \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1} \\,\\textrm d t =-\\int_0^x \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1}\\,\\textrm d t\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\displaystyle\\dfrac {\\textrm d} {\\textrm dx} \\int_x^0 \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1} \\,\\textrm d t & \\, \\, = \\, \\, \\dfrac {\\textrm d} {\\textrm dx} \\left(-\\int_0^x \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1} \\,\\textrm d t \\right) \\\\ & \\, \\, = \\, \\, -\\dfrac {\\textrm d} {\\textrm dx} \\left(\\int_0^x \\dfrac{t^3}{t^2 +1} \\,\\textrm d t \\right) \\\\ &= \\, \\, -\\dfrac{x^3}{x^2 +1}. \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534913 false] [17592186078235 1100 "Find $f'(x)$ for $f(x) = \\displaystyle \\int_2^{x^2}\\arctan t\\,\\textrm d t$." 13194139534913 false] [17592186078235 1100 "Find $f'(x)$ for $f(x) = \\displaystyle \\int_2^{x^2}\\arctan t\\,\\textrm d t.$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186078235 1145 "To compute $f'(x)$, we first make the substitution $u=x^2$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}∫_{2}^{x^{2}}\\arctan tdt \\\\\n&= \\frac{du}{dx} \\cdot \\frac{d}{du}∫_{2}^{u}\\arctan tdt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous for all $t$, so by FTC II we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{du}{dx} \\cdot \\arctan (u) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2}) \\cdot \\arctan (u) \\\\\n&= 2x\\arctan (x^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534913 false] [17592186078235 1145 "To compute $f'(x),$  we first make the substitution $u=x^2$  and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{2}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{du}}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{2}^{u}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe integrand is continuous for all $t,$ so by FTC II we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(u) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186078236 1100 "Find $f'(1)$ if  $\\displaystyle f(x) = \\int_x^{x^2} (t^2 + 2t)  \\,\\, \\textrm d t.$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186078236 1100 "Find $f'(1)$ if $\\displaystyle f(x) = \\int_x^{x^2} (t^2 + 2t) \\,\\, \\textrm d t$." 13194139534913 false] [17592186078236 1145 "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{x}^{x^{2}}(t^{2} + 2t)dt &= ∫_{x}^{a}(t^{2} + 2t)dt + ∫_{a}^{x^{2}}(t^{2} + 2t)dt \\\\\n&= - ∫_{a}^{x}(t^{2} + 2t)dt + ∫_{a}^{x^{2}}(t^{2} + 2t)dt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $x$ and $x^2$.\n\nThe integrand $t^2 + 2t$ is continuous for all $t$, so applying FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(- ∫_{a}^{x}(t^{2} + 2t)dt + ∫_{a}^{x^{2}}(t^{2} + 2t)dt) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{d}{dx}(∫_{a}^{x}(t^{2} + 2t)dt) + \\frac{d}{dx}(∫_{a}^{x^{2}}(t^{2} + 2t)dt) \\\\\n&= - (x^{2} + 2x) + \\frac{du}{dx}\\frac{d}{du}(∫_{a}^{u}(t^{2} + 2t)dt) \\\\\n&=-x^{2} - 2x + 2x(u^{2} + 2u) \\\\\n&=-x^{2} - 2x + 2x((x^{2})^{2} + 2x^{2}) \\\\\n&=-x^{2} - 2x + 2x(x^{4} + 2x^{2}) \\\\\n&=-x^{2} - 2x + 2x^{5} + 4x^{3} \\\\\n&= 2x^{5} + 4x^{3} - x^{2} - 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=x^2$, as before.\n\nFinally, we can compute $f'(1)$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(1) &= 2(1)^{5} + 4(1)^{3} - (1)^{2} - 2(1) \\\\\n&= 2 + 4 - 1 - 2 \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534913 false] [17592186078236 1145 "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{x}^{{x}^{2}}({t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{x}^{a}({t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{{x}^{2}}({t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{x}({t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{{x}^{2}}({t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $x$ and $x^2.$\n\nThe integrand $t^2 + 2t$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{x}({t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{{x}^{2}}({t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}({t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{{x}^{2}}({t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2x)+\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}({t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-2x+2x({u}^{2}+2u) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-2x+2x(({x}^{2})^{2}+2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-2x+2x({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-2x+2{x}^{5}+4{x}^{3} \\\\  & =2{x}^{5}+4{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=x^2,$ as before.\n\nFinally, we can compute $f'(1).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =2(1)^{5}+4(1)^{3}-(1)^{2}-2(1) \\\\  & =2+4-1-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186078357 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319285 13194139534913 true] [17592186078357 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319299 13194139534913 true] [17592186078357 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319306 13194139534913 true] [17592186078357 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319372 13194139534913 true] [17592186078358 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319313 13194139534913 true] [17592186078358 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319316 13194139534913 true] [17592186078358 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319324 13194139534913 true] [17592186078358 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319328 13194139534913 true] [17592186078358 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319358 13194139534913 true] [17592186078359 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319320 13194139534913 true] [17592186078359 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319331 13194139534913 true] [17592186078359 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319334 13194139534913 true] [17592186078359 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319344 13194139534913 true] [17592186078359 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319351 13194139534913 true] [17592186078360 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319292 13194139534913 true] [17592186078360 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319337 13194139534913 true] [17592186078360 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319340 13194139534913 true] [17592186078360 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319365 13194139534913 true] [17592186078858 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534913 true] [17592186078858 1100 "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{3}^{x}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{{t}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}t$ for $x>3.$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186078858 1100 "Calculate $\\frac{d}{dx}∫_{3}^{x}\\frac{\\cos t}{t^{2} + 4}dt$ for $x > 3$." 13194139534913 false] [17592186078858 1145 "The function $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{{t}^{2}+4}$ is continuous on $[3,x],$ where $x>3.$ So, FTC II applies, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{3}^{x}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{{t}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319285 1017 #edb/ref 17592186319286 13194139534913 true] [17592186319285 1089 "q-116475" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319285 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534913 true] [17592186319285 1100 "If $g(x)={\\int }_{0}^{x}{t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t$ for $x>0,$ determine ${g}^{′}(2).$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319285 1113 #uuid "8f0f42de-b5f1-5a07-8a0d-c5f6caca1908" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319285 1145 "The function ${t}^{2}{e}^{t}$ is continuous on $[0,x],$ where $x>0.$ So, FTC II applies, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of ${g}^{′}(2),$ we substitute $x=2$ in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(2) & ={2}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{2} \\\\  & =4{e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319287 13194139534913 true] [17592186319286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319288 13194139534913 true] [17592186319286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319289 13194139534913 true] [17592186319286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319290 13194139534913 true] [17592186319286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319291 13194139534913 true] [17592186319286 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534913 true] [17592186319286 1041 "selection" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319286 1104 #edb/ref 17592186319291 13194139534913 true] [17592186319286 1110 #uuid "96e0731b-1d21-5e11-83d4-edbd8703284c" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319287 1034 "2{e}^{2}" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534913 true] [17592186319287 1111 #uuid "71c1f60e-96ea-55f2-a5f2-b7e0973c6272" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319288 1034 "8e" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534913 true] [17592186319288 1111 #uuid "adf9fa8b-0215-5d18-98fd-abc4fc8d1a49" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319289 1034 "e" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534913 true] [17592186319289 1111 #uuid "06090104-7633-5e00-9938-e3bbd7c27ece" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319290 1034 "1" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534913 true] [17592186319290 1111 #uuid "2368dcd8-f3de-5a02-8f0f-c92165ec8e8e" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319291 1034 "4{e}^{2}" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534913 true] [17592186319291 1111 #uuid "0c649abc-e469-5ae7-92e0-4558cc6103cc" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319292 1017 #edb/ref 17592186319293 13194139534913 true] [17592186319292 1089 "q-117289" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319292 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534913 true] [17592186319292 1100 "Find ${f}^{′}(1)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319292 1113 #uuid "1a5fda93-db37-5201-9a1b-f45b1acfcd5a" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319292 1145 "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{x}^{a}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $x$ and $\\sqrt{x}.$\n\nThe integrand $\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+3}+\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+3}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{u}^{4}+3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+3}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}((\\sqrt{x})^{4}+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}({x}^{2}+3)}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(1).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1}({1}^{2}+3)}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{4}+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319294 13194139534913 true] [17592186319293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319295 13194139534913 true] [17592186319293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319296 13194139534913 true] [17592186319293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319297 13194139534913 true] [17592186319293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319298 13194139534913 true] [17592186319293 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534913 true] [17592186319293 1041 "selection" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319293 1104 #edb/ref 17592186319294 13194139534913 true] [17592186319293 1110 #uuid "05575e57-4021-5a57-b22c-aa88d47b637a" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319294 1034 "-\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319294 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534913 true] [17592186319294 1111 #uuid "94e7b54e-df1b-564b-b397-7d7a260ed3d3" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319295 1034 "-\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534913 true] [17592186319295 1111 #uuid "c9e568fc-550a-5922-ace2-4495328f1423" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319296 1034 "\\frac{3}{8}" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534913 true] [17592186319296 1111 #uuid "04bfafa5-fff9-51cb-b195-6f5f762d519a" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319297 1034 "0" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319297 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534913 true] [17592186319297 1111 #uuid "99a92494-e0cf-52de-ab02-c000b4dbf8c7" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319298 1034 "-1" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534913 true] [17592186319298 1111 #uuid "7e7753f8-282c-5360-ba7a-676831fb28da" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319