\n\nThe integrand $\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}}$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{du}}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{x}{2+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{u}{2+{u}^{2}})+\\frac{x}{2+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{2+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}})+\\frac{x}{2+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2+{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{2x+x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x).$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${F}^{′}(e).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(e) & =\\frac{e}{2+{e}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡e}{2e+e(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{2+{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2e+e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{2+{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{3e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319367 13194139534913 true] [17592186319366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319368 13194139534913 true] [17592186319366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319369 13194139534913 true] [17592186319366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319370 13194139534913 true] [17592186319366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319371 13194139534913 true] [17592186319366 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534913 true] [17592186319366 1041 "selection" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319366 1104 #edb/ref 17592186319368 13194139534913 true] [17592186319366 1110 #uuid "a59c82ba-af0b-5b0e-8ff5-2ec31d060609" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319367 1034 "\\frac{e}{2+{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{3}}" 13194139534913 true] [17592186319367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 